member.summary:
Allows you to set a delegate that will control the mouse movement from the current mouse position to a destination position.
The delegate contains 3 parameters:
Vector2i destination: The final mouse position desired.
Vector2i normalizedDestination: The final mouse position, confined in the game window (this is equal to destination in case the position is already inside the window)
Vector2i currentPosition: The actual mouse position.

It is your duty to eventually set the debugMouse position, and actually move the mouse.
This is what the original code look like:

 {
    // Set the internal mouse thread position.
    // This is actually not used, but might become a standard soon™ so do not forget to set this 2 parms every time you move the mouse.
    MousePoseX = normalizedDestination.X;
    MousePoseY = normalizedDestination.Y;
    
    // If the DebugCursor is enabled, move the actual mouse to the correct screen position.
    if (DebugCursor)
    {
       var mousepos = LokiPoe.Utility.MousePosToScreenPosAbsoluteDebug(normalizedPos);
       Framework.WinApi.SetCursorPos(mousepos.X, mousepos.Y);
    }
    // Set the Hook mouse position, and and add the mouse movement to the system message queue. (this 2 functions are what actually move the mouse)
    SetMouseHookPosition(normalizedPos);
    PostMouseMovement(MousePoseX, MousePoseY, sleep);
 }

Return the number of monsters remaining in the current area.
Pls Note: if the return is 51, it mean that more than 50 monsters are remaining it can be any number, the server start to give you exact number only when less that 51 monsters are remaining.
if the return is 255, it mean that the  current map do not support this feature. (town or scenary map)

 Looks up a localized string similar to [
